detaileddescription.para:
@thread_safe Safe to call from any thread
Blocking: Waits for auto-rotation thread to join
Exception-safe: Destructor does not throw

LEK key_id suitable for use with FieldEncryption::encryptField() Format: "lek_<YYYY-MM-DD>" 



std::runtime_error



if LEK generation or storage fails



@thread_safe Yes - internally synchronized 
Automatic generation: If no LEK exists for today, one is created 


Idempotent: Calling multiple times returns the same key_id

Usage: std::stringlek_id=lek_mgr->getCurrentLEK();
field_enc.encryptField("user_email","alice@example.com",lek_id);

Usage: std::stringold_lek=lek_mgr->getLEKForDate("2026-08-01");
if(!old_lek.empty()){
autodecrypted=field_enc.decryptField(encrypted_data,old_lek);
}

@thread_safe Yes - internally synchronized 

std::runtime_error



if LEK creation fails




Effect: Next getCurrentLEK() returns the new key 


Audit: Rotation event is logged if AuditLogger is attached

Usage: //Securityincident:forcekeyrotation
lek_mgr->rotate();
//AllsubsequentencryptionsusenewLEK

Vector of revoked dates in "YYYY-MM-DD" format @thread_safe Yes

Usage: autorevoked=lek_mgr->getRevokedKeys();
for(constauto&date:revoked){
LOG(INFO)<<"Revoked:"<<date;
}
